BT
/F10 12 Tf
13.7999999999999989 TL
0.059 0.09 0.165 rg
56.6929133858267775 728.7876377952756002 Td
(2.4 Supervised Learning in Financial Security) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.118 g
56.6929133858267775 711.7797637795275705 Td
(Supervised binary classification represents the established industry benchmark for fraud detection when historical) Tj
T* (labeled transaction databases are accessible. The primary strength of supervised learning is its direct optimization) Tj
T* (against known fraudulent behaviors. [Reference to be Added]) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.118 g
56.6929133858267775 661.0396062992125508 Td
(However, supervised training in financial transaction security faces unique domain challenges. The primary obstacle is) Tj
T* (the extreme rarity of fraudulent events compared to normal commercial activities, alongside non-stationary consumer) Tj
T* (spending distributions \(covariate shift\). Models must generalize without overfitting to historic attack patterns that) Tj
T* (fraudsters have already abandoned. [Reference to be Added]) Tj
ET
BT
/F10 12 Tf
13.7999999999999989 TL
0.059 0.09 0.165 rg
56.6929133858267775 591.0238582677164914 Td
(2.5 Class Imbalance in Fraud Detection) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.118 g
56.6929133858267775 574.0159842519684616 Td
(A pervasive characteristic of financial transaction datasets is extreme class imbalance. In legitimate banking networks,) Tj
T* (fraudulent transactions typically constitute less than 0.1% to 1% of total transaction volume. [Reference to be Added]) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.118 g
56.6929133858267775 536.8821259842519567 Td
(When standard machine learning classifiers \(such as traditional decision trees or unweighted logistic regression\) are) Tj
T* (fitted on heavily skewed data, they optimize for overall accuracy. A naive model that classifies 100% of transactions as) Tj
T* ("Legitimate" will effortlessly achieve 99.9% classification accuracy while failing to detect a single fraudulent) Tj
T* (transaction. [Reference to be Added]) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.118 g
56.6929133858267775 472.5356692913385928 Td
(To address this failure mode, literature documents two primary strategies: resampling techniques \(such as SMOTE) Tj
T* (oversampling or random undersampling\) and algorithmic cost-sensitive weighting. Resampling can introduce synthetic) Tj
T* (artifacts or discard valuable majority-class information. Conversely, cost-sensitive learningósuch as computing) Tj
T* (class-balanced sample weightsóadjusts the loss function penalty proportionally to class frequencies, forcing the) Tj
T* (optimization algorithm to heavily penalize errors on minority fraud cases without distorting the underlying empirical) Tj
T* (feature distribution. [Reference to be Added]) Tj
ET
BT
/F10 12 Tf
13.7999999999999989 TL
0.059 0.09 0.165 rg
56.6929133858267775 375.3073228346457313 Td
(2.6 Categorical Feature Encoding) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.118 g
56.6929133858267775 358.2994488188976447 Td
(Financial transaction records contain rich categorical information, including merchant identifiers, merchant categories,) Tj
T* (customer state, city, and occupation. Traditional preprocessing methods such as One-Hot Encoding \(OHE\) become) Tj
T* (mathematically intractable when applied to high-cardinality features. For instance, a dataset containing 5,000 distinct) Tj
T* (merchants would expand the feature matrix by 5,000 sparse columns, triggering the curse of dimensionality, immense) Tj
T* (RAM consumption, and severe tree overfitting. [Reference to be Added]) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.118 g
56.6929133858267775 280.346692913385823 Td
(Label Encoding assigns arbitrary integers \(e.g., 1, 2, 3\), which inadvertently imposes a false ordinal hierarchy upon) Tj
T* (unordered categories. Target Encoding computes the mean target value for each categorical level, but naive target) Tj
T* (encoding causes severe target leakage and overfitting on training folds.) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.118 g
56.6929133858267775 229.606535433070917 Td
(CatBoost Encoding resolves these vulnerabilities by calculating target statistics using an ordered principle. It computes) Tj
T* (the posterior probability of the target based on prior records in a randomized sequence, regularized with an empirical) Tj
T* (prior. This provides a robust, low-dimensional continuous representation for high-cardinality categories that preserves) Tj
T* (predictive power while preventing data leakage. [Reference to be Added]) Tj
ET
BT
/F10 12 Tf
13.7999999999999989 TL
