(Gradient Boosted Decision Trees \(GBDT\) are recognized as the state-of-the-art algorithmic family for tabular and) Tj
T* (structured financial datasets. Popular implementations such as XGBoost, LightGBM, and CatBoost iteratively construct) Tj
T* (an ensemble of shallow decision trees, where each subsequent tree fits to the pseudo-residuals \(gradients\) of the loss) Tj
T* (function from previous trees. [Reference to be Added]) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.118 g
56.6929133858267775 720.8506299212598378 Td
(Scikit-learnís HistGradientBoostingClassifier represents an optimized modern GBDT variant inspired by LightGBM.) Tj
T* (Instead of sorting continuous feature values at every split candidateówhich incurs an O\(n_samples * log\(n_samples\)\)) Tj
T* (computational costóHistGradientBoosting bins continuous numerical values into 256 discrete integer bins) Tj
T* (\(histograms\). This reduces split evaluation complexity to O\(n_bins\), accelerating training by orders of magnitude while) Tj
T* (reducing memory footprint and offering native regularized tree growth. [Reference to be Added]) Tj
ET
BT
/F10 12 Tf
13.7999999999999989 TL
