(3.1 Existing System) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.118 g
56.6929133858267775 694.4884251968503577 Td
(The existing credit card fraud screening mechanisms implemented across many regional financial cooperatives and) Tj
T* (mid-tier retail merchants rely upon legacy batch audits and static, rules-based screening filters.) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.118 g
56.6929133858267775 657.3545669291338527 Td
(In these systems, transactions are evaluated sequentially against a flat configuration file containing boolean constraints.) Tj
T* (If a transaction amount exceeds an arbitrary threshold, or if the country of origin differs from the domestic home bank,) Tj
T* (the transaction is routed into a manual review queue or declined outright. Secondary audits are conducted post-facto) Tj
T* (\(often 24 to 72 hours following transaction settlement\) through human investigative review of end-of-day ledger) Tj
T* (reports.) Tj
ET
BT
/F10 12 Tf
13.7999999999999989 TL
0.059 0.09 0.165 rg
56.6929133858267775 573.7325196850392786 Td
(3.2 Problems in Existing System) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.118 g
56.6929133858267775 556.7246456692912489 Td
(Analysis of the existing operational framework reveals several fatal deficiencies:) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.118 g
56.6929133858267775 533.1970866141732586 Td
(ï High Operational Latency: Post-settlement manual audits fail to prevent fraud in real time. By the time an investigator) Tj
T* (identifies a compromised card, multiple fraudulent purchases have already cleared.) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.118 g
56.6929133858267775 496.0632283464566967 Td
(ï Excessive False Decline Rates: Legitimate customer transactions that violate rigid rules are blocked, causing) Tj
T* (significant customer embarrassment, brand defection, and merchant lost revenue.) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.118 g
56.6929133858267775 458.9293700787401349 Td
(ï Labor-Intensive Workflow: Financial institutions must maintain extensive teams of fraud analysts to manually inspect) Tj
T* (large queues of flagged transactions, resulting in unsustainable operational expenditure.) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.118 g
56.6929133858267775 421.795511811023573 Td
(ï Susceptibility to Human Fatigue and Error: Human analysts processing hundreds of routine records daily are prone to) Tj
T* (oversight, missing intricate non-linear attack vectors.) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.118 g
56.6929133858267775 384.661653543307068 Td
(ï Inability to Calculate Calibrated Risk: Existing systems provide binary \(Pass/Fail\) outcomes rather than a nuanced,) Tj
T* (continuous probability score that reflects the degree of suspicion.) Tj
ET
BT
/F10 12 Tf
13.7999999999999989 TL
0.059 0.09 0.165 rg
56.6929133858267775 341.8585039370078675 Td
(3.3 Proposed System) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.118 g
56.6929133858267775 324.8506299212598378 Td
(To overcome the structural weaknesses of the existing paradigm, this project introduces CreditGuard AI ó an) Tj
T* (end-to-end, machine-learning-powered credit card fraud detection web application.) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.118 g
56.6929133858267775 287.7167716535433328 Td
(The proposed system receives transaction telemetry via an intuitive, fintech-styled web interface, validates all incoming) Tj
T* (inputs, derives rich temporal and geospatial features, transforms high-cardinality categorical inputs using a fitted) Tj
T* (CatBoostEncoder, and feeds the numerical feature vector into a trained HistGradientBoostingClassifier.) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.118 g
56.6929133858267775 236.9766141732283131 Td
(The classifier computes the exact posterior probability that the transaction belongs to the fraudulent class. This) Tj
T* (probability is compared against a calibrated threshold of 0.90 to produce a definitive risk classification \(Legitimate vs.) Tj
T* (Potentially Fraudulent\), which is rendered back to the user within milliseconds alongside comprehensive diagnostic) Tj
T* (metrics.) Tj
ET
BT
/F10 12 Tf
13.7999999999999989 TL
