(6.5 Fraud Decision Threshold Configuration \(Threshold = 0.90\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.118 g
56.6929133858267775 613.9844881889763428 Td
(Standard binary classification implementations assign class labels based on a default 0.50 probability cutoff \(i.e., if) Tj
T* (P\(Fraud\) >= 0.50, flag as fraud\). However, in financial risk systems, a 0.50 threshold frequently leads to an) Tj
T* (unacceptable volume of false positives, irritating valuable cardholders and overwhelming operational review desks.) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.118 g
56.6929133858267775 563.2443307086613231 Td
(To ensure that only transactions exhibiting overwhelming anomalies and extreme statistical deviation are flagged as) Tj
T* (fraud, CreditGuard AI adopts a strict probability decision threshold of 0.90:) Tj
ET
0.96 0.97 0.98 rg
56.6929133858267775 534.614409448818833 481.8941732283464034 -24.0944881889763813 re
f
